emediation for deterministic P10/P6 findings: added a `## Testing` section that mirrors all existing ticket-level verify commands and split compound acceptance criteria into independently observable outcomes. No implementation target, public-description scope, typed default/coercion contract, or runtime behavior changed.","timestamp":1787420577450123001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for blocking E6/F1 finding: added a row-by-row manual editorial proof that compares each Description cell with its Key, Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells and requires the completed review to be recorded on the ticket. Also clarified that F19 authorizes the follow-on Description column, documented the single-source rationale for field metadata, and split the remaining compound criteria. No automated content heuristic or runtime change was added.","timestamp":1787421279853084001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third plan-review remediation for blocking E6/F1 finding: marked the four editorial criteria `[non-codebase]` and bound their manual proof to a ticket comment containing reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and the completed row-by-row result. Also made the missing/empty-metadata failure-injection test explicit and clarified that `public_description` is the authoritative external prose while existing comments remain internal notes. Scope remains configuration-documentation generation only; runtime behavior is unchanged.","timestamp":1787421890547400001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution preflight counted 100 emitted fields in the 697-line schema module. Adding required field metadata in place would put formatting headroom at risk under the absolute 800-line limit. Recorded  as the exact section-boundary extraction named by the approved plan and expanded the module-size proof to cover both schema modules. This material correction intentionally invalidates the prior F19B attestation and its parent material pin.","timestamp":1787423913935762001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction. The exact extraction path is src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py. The preceding comment lost that path when its shell quoting interpreted Markdown backticks. The five-path file-impact event and four verification commands contain the correct value.","timestamp":1787423938051679001}],"created_at":1787417361912923001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration reference enumerates key, type, default, and lifecycle data from typed dataclass fields but provides no public setting descriptions. It cannot serve as the external settings contract until each emitted key explains its user-visible effect. F19 explicitly authorizes this Description-column enrichment as corrective follow-on scope beyond the closed generator baseline; generated ownership remains unchanged.\n\n## Plan\n- Add concise `public_description` metadata to every dataclass field emitted through `_SECTION_CLASSES`, co-located with each field so generator introspection remains the single source of truth and a sidecar description registry cannot drift.\n- Treat `public_description` as the authoritative external setting prose; existing code comments remain internal implementation notes rather than a second generated contract.\n- Preserve field types, defaults, factories, coercion, and runtime behavior.\n- Extend `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` to require nonempty description metadata and render a Description column.\n- Fail generation when an emitted field lacks a description.\n- Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md`.\n- Add focused tests for complete metadata, table escaping, generated drift, and an injected missing or empty description that fails with the offending key named.\n- Review every generated Description cell against its key plus adjacent Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells; require a user-visible effect or operational consequence rather than a restatement, then record the reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and completed row-by-row result in a ticket comment.\n- Keep `src/rebar` modules below the absolute 800-line limit. Use an existing configuration-section seam if an extraction is required.\n\n## Testing\n- `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py -q`\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt)`\n- `make lint && make typecheck`\n- Manual non-codebase proof: inspect every generated Description row against its Key, Type, Default, and Lifecycle cells; record reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and the completed row-by-row result in a ticket comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every generated typed key has one nonempty public description.\n- [ ] The injected missing or empty metadata test fails with the offending key named.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Each description identifies a user-visible effect or operational consequence, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row type, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row default, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] No description merely restates its row lifecycle, attested by the named and timestamped row review.\n- [ ] Generated Markdown escapes table-sensitive content correctly.\n- [ ] Typed field annotations remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Default values remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Default factories remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Configuration coercion remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Configuration runtime behavior remains unchanged.\n- [ ] `_config_schema.py` remains within the absolute module-size limit.\n- [ ] Focused generator tests pass.\n- [ ] Focused typed-configuration tests pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Type checking passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Attach public descriptions to typed configuration fields and import the extracted VerifyConfig section."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py","reason":"Hold the extracted VerifyConfig dataclass and its field description metadata within the module-size policy."},{"path":"scripts/gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Require and render public descriptions."},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"Regenerate configuration rows with descriptions."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py","reason":"Pin description completeness, escaping, and drift behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","66c6-2fe5-4850-4297"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"66c6-2fe5-4850-4297","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["documentation","f19b","configuration"],"ticket_id":"5df8-2209-2c49-42c8","ticket_type":"task","title":"F19B generate descriptions for every typed configuration key","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Generated configuration reference is current"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py tests/unit/test_config_typed.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py -q","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Description and typed configuration contracts pass"},{"command":"python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt) && test $(wc -l < src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py) -le $(cat .github/module-size-limit.txt)","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Complexity and module-size contracts pass for both schema modules"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck","dd_id":"D4","dd_text":"Source lint and type checks pass"}]},"source_event_uuids":["c74514be-de91-42e6-a7a0-ee8041d3258b","3a2884cf-4932-4e96-9494-d54e8b8d0afb","3d511cf6-ef4e-4e3b-b711-f1b851b70c52","13f757fa-e302-4029-8d35-554f9d0a74f9","5d8fdb80-da0d-413d-8d27-8b1be78411c5","584dfd4b-9ffa-487b-8e36-9f83c5e93a8a","8f8b4f34-2dee-4229-98d2-9cf56e49db26","3067149d-7179-484a-9ca2-f51502fe2658","a8411f3e-7722-4f6e-9c17-cdc33a3e16c9","bbfabc68-fb49-48da-a1fb-ccca7c060f73","4c44e63a-c2c0-48a0-bef0-e62f01a1e843","a02a39ac-ae23-4348-9445-0e924e32ddd0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787423938051679002,"uuid":"8d9875a0-00d6-4071-b699-4b1c687ed1e3"}